ability, but still maintain vote. Could also bring up Candidate A's strengths vs concerns. But we need to reference existing discussion.\n\nWe have no new info. We could ask for more info on B's decision quality or adaptability, but that would be a tool call. However we already asked earlier and got no info. Could ask about Candidate D's crew cooperation? But we already have no info. The panel still missing info on several criteria. But we need to make a contribution now.\n\nGiven the instruction, we should make a focused argumentative contribution, stating current recommendation. We can say we still recommend B, but note that we need concrete examples of decision quality and adaptability, but given the lack, we still think B is best relative to others.\n\nWe can also bring up Candidate A's egocentric and unwillingness to further education as a bigger risk than B's interpersonal style.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Agent 1 and 2, still vote B, because B's reliability, stress handling, technical competence outweigh A's communication issues, C's unfriendly and unknown stress resilience, D's moodiness and loner.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills; concerns: pretentious, wrong tone, nasty remarks. A: 100% reliable, quick correct decisions, excellent attention, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. C: unfriendly, etc. D: moody, loner.\n\nThus final."}
